---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import UtilityLab from '../components/UtilityLab.jsx';
---

<Layout
  title="Lab — Production Patterns, Rebuilt in the Open | Nikhil Raj PK"
  description="Sanitized public rebuilds of four GTM patterns that already run in production: enrichment waterfall, procurement signal harvesting, inbound routing and LLM account qualification."
>
  <main id="main" class="overflow-x-clip">
    <header class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 pt-32 md:pt-44 pb-14 md:pb-20 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-end">
      <div class="lg:col-span-8">
        <span class="kicker mb-8">GTM Systems Lab</span>
        <h1 class="display" data-reveal="wipe">
          Production patterns, <br /><span class="italic text-stone-400">rebuilt in the open.</span>
        </h1>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-4" data-reveal style="--d:150ms">
        <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
          Each of these systems already runs in production — their full breakdowns are in <a href="/work" class="underline decoration-zapier underline-offset-4 hover:text-zapier">Work</a>. The lab versions are sanitized rebuilds I'm publishing so the code itself can be read.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- How to read the labels -->
    <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 pb-12" aria-label="Status labels">
      <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 border-t border-stone-200 text-sm" data-reveal>
        <div class="py-5 md:pr-8 border-b border-stone-200">
          <dt class="flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold"><span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-zapier"></span>Proven in production</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1.5 text-stone-600">The pattern itself runs in a live system. Each card links to it.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="py-5 md:px-8 border-b border-stone-200 md:border-l">
          <dt class="font-semibold">Public rebuild in progress</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1.5 text-stone-600">A sanitized version is being written. The public code isn't ready yet.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="py-5 md:pl-8 border-b border-stone-200 md:border-l">
          <dt class="font-semibold">Public rebuild queued</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1.5 text-stone-600">Not started. "In progress" or "queued" never means the pattern is unproven.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <UtilityLab client:load />

    <!-- Where the patterns went -->
    <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="border-y border-stone-200 py-10 md:py-14 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-center">
        <h2 class="lg:col-span-6 font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[1.02] tracking-tight" data-reveal>
          The same patterns, <span class="italic text-stone-400">under bigger systems.</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="lg:col-span-6" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
          <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
            Enrichment and qualification sit inside the lead-generation console. The signal harvester's collect, de-duplicate and review loop also runs under tender discovery, a procurement research pilot and a job-discovery tool.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-3">
            <a href="/systems#compose-collection" class="link-arrow">
              One collection pattern, four uses
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17 17 7M8 7h9v9" /></svg>
            </a>
            <a href="/systems#compose-sales" class="link-arrow">
              The full sales system
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17 17 7M8 7h9v9" /></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 pb-24 md:pb-32">
      <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 max-w-2xl" data-reveal>
        The small panels inside each card are interactive illustrations of the pattern, not live connections to production data.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
